                <pb facs="0297" n="201" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg201"/>

                <head>No. 157.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bolt
                        to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gaspé,
                                Quebec</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-06-21"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 21, 1872</date>.
                        (Received June 21.)</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hamilton Eish</hi>:</p>
                <p>The scandalous action of hoisting the Dominion flag over the American, on the
                    schooner James Bliss, is repeated this morning, and remains so.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>GEO. HOLT, <hi rendition="#italic">Consul.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
